      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am able to reproduce this consistently in FISH! across restarts.\n\nSee performance sampling data from output logs on VRChat 2026.4.1p3 (Build `1939` and VRChat 2026.4.2 (Build `1953`) attached, at 2026.11.26 15:05:15 and 2026.11.26 15:05:18, both in a FISH! world, an uncontrolled A/B identical scene for ~5 minutes.\n\nGLM-5.3-Flash prompt:\n\n```\n\nExample 1:\n\n[paste of 2026.4.1p3 Performance Stats]\n\nExample 2:\n\n[paste of 2026.4.2 Performance Stats]\n\nHas anything changed in performance?\n\n```\n\nGLM-5.3-Flash's response summarized:\n\n- **FPS (mean / time-weighted)**: 105.2 / 102.8 → 78.1 / 74.7 **(−26%)**\n\n- **CPU time**: 8.7 ms → 12.4 ms **(+42%)**\n\n- **Input latency (mean)**: 9.1 ms → 12.5 ms **(+38%)**\n\n- GPU frame time (mean): 0.71 ms → 0.73 ms (~unchanged)\n\n- Ping: 46 ms → 49.5 ms (+8% (minor))\n\n- Managed memory (mean / peak): 828 MB / 880 MB →869 MB / 988 MB (+5% / +12%)\n\n- Texture memory total: 554 MB → 498 MB (−10%)\n\n- Net bytes \"66\" per frame unchanged.\n\n- Avatar (polys / bones / materials) unchanged (Good avatar).",
